# Help & i18n lock (D230)

Whenever you **add or deepen a user-facing feature** (module, screen, action, portal flow):

## Mandatory before marking the lot done

1. **Help catalog** — update [`apps/web/src/lib/help-guide-catalog.ts`](apps/web/src/lib/help-guide-catalog.ts):
   - Add or extend the relevant `HELP_MODULES` entry
   - Include: summary · when · feature name · when · **step-by-step** (FR + IT)
   - Add `locks` if Prefs / legal / Soft Glass constraints apply
2. **Italian overlays** (FR is source of truth):
   - New chrome / button / empty-state strings → `UI_STRINGS_IT` in `apps/web/src/lib/i18n/route-labels.ts`
   - New module / feature registry labels → `MODULE_LABELS_IT` / `FEATURE_LABELS_IT` in `registry-labels.ts`
   - Status labels → `status-labels.ts` if applicable
3. **Do not** leave Help stale for “later” — same lot as the feature.

## Out of scope for Help

- Pure refactors with no UX change
- Internal API-only changes with zero UI surface
- Super Admin control-plane unless it gains an operator-facing screen

## Language chrome

- Locale toggle = **Languages** icon (globe) — never hardcode `IT | FR` text in the topbar.
